  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": ".NET 9 and C# 13 locking",
      "items": [
        "C# 13 and .NET 9 introduced the dedicated `System.Threading.Lock` type and compiler-aware lowering for the `lock` statement. When the expression is statically typed as `System.Threading.Lock`, the compiler uses `EnterScope`; ordinary object locks continue to use Monitor semantics. .NET 6 added `Parallel.ForEachAsync` for bounded asynchronous loop bodies."
      ],
